    {
      "id": "concept-airline-seat-map-cockpit-selection",
      "kind": "concept",
      "promptEs": "selección de asiento · diagrama del avión · clic en la cabina",
      "questionEn": "What visual mistake creates the joke?",
      "answerEn": "The passenger treats the cockpit drawn on an airline seat map as a selectable seat, so clicking it puts her in the pilot's position.",
      "noteEn": "Real airline diagrams show the aircraft around the passenger seats but do not make the cockpit selectable. The final panel turns the interface click into a literal assignment to fly the plane. The title text extends the same absurd interface rule to the wing.",
